+# Proposal
+
+## Why
+
+Deleting a discontinued product currently leaves carts and order-read paths dependent on a live catalog row, so previously valid carts and orders fail or lose their history. Merchants need product deletion to remove only the active catalog item while preserving cart usability and the immutable details of completed purchases.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Make cart reads, recalculation, updates, multi-item operations, and checkout tolerate deleted products by removing deleted cart lines and recalculating quantity, subtotal, total, and order contents from the remaining lines.
+- Return HTTP 404 when an add-to-cart request or v2 product lookup targets a deleted product.
+- Preserve order-product snapshot fields (SKU, name, quantity, unit price, subtotal, and related presentation data) so all merchant and customer order endpoints remain readable after catalog deletion.
+- Keep persisted order totals and status updates independent of the deleted catalog product.
+- Add regression coverage for mixed and product-only carts, add-to-cart and lookup 404s, checkout, all order read paths, order status changes, and isolation of other products.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+
+- `product-deletion-resilience`: Deleted catalog products no longer break carts or historical orders, while active-product and not-found behavior remains explicit.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+None.
+
+## Impact
+
+Likely affected areas are the shopping-cart service/facade/populators and calculation path, product lookup and delete controllers/services, order-product persistence and read mappers/populators, checkout flow, and integration tests in `sm-shop` plus relevant core model/service tests. The public API contract changes only by making the specified deleted-product cases return 404 and by making existing cart/order endpoints resilient.
